@startuml Weaver Test Execution - Complete Flow

!define TEST_COLOR #3498DB
!define OTEL_COLOR #9B59B6
!define WEAVER_COLOR #E74C3C
!define SUCCESS_COLOR #2ECC71
!define FAIL_COLOR #FF6B6B

title clnrm Test Execution with Weaver Validation - Complete Flow

actor "Developer" as Dev
participant "Test Suite" as Tests
participant "OTel SDK" as SDK
participant "Batch\nProcessor" as Batch
participant "OTLP\nExporter" as Exporter
participant "Weaver\nlive-check\n:4317" as Weaver
participant "Built-in\nAdvisors" as Advisors
participant "Statistics\nGenerator" as Stats
participant "CI/CD\nGate" as Gate

== Initialization Phase ==

Dev -> Tests : cargo test --features otel
activate Tests #TEST_COLOR

Tests -> SDK : init_otel(config)
activate SDK #OTEL_COLOR

note right of SDK
    **CRITICAL CONFIG:**
    ```rust
    OtelConfig {
        export: Export::OtlpGrpc {
            endpoint: "http://localhost:4317"
        },
        // NOT StdoutNdjson!
    }
    ```
end note

SDK -> Batch : create_batch_processor()
activate Batch

SDK -> Exporter : create_otlp_grpc_exporter()
activate Exporter

Exporter -> Weaver : TCP connect :4317
activate Weaver #WEAVER_COLOR

Weaver --> Exporter : Connection established
note right
    Weaver starts at test begin:
    ```bash
    weaver registry live-check \
      --registry registry/ \
      --otlp-grpc-port 4317 \
      --format json \
      --output validation_output/
    ```
end note

== Test Execution Phase ==

loop For each test

    Tests -> Tests : test_container_execution()
    note right #TEST_COLOR
        ```rust
        #[tokio::test]
        async fn test_container_execution() {
            let env = CleanroomEnvironment::new().await?;

            // This creates a span automatically
            let result = env.execute_in_container(
                "test_container",
                &["echo", "hello"]
            ).await?;

            assert_eq!(result.exit_code, 0);
        }
        ```
    end note

    Tests -> SDK : tracer.start_span("test_execution")
    SDK -> SDK : create span

    Tests -> Tests : execute_in_container()
    note right
        Creates real Docker container.
        Executes command.
        Captures output.
    end note

    Tests -> SDK : span.set_attribute("container.id", real_id)
    Tests -> SDK : span.set_attribute("test.isolated", true)
    Tests -> SDK : span.set_attribute("command", "echo hello")
    Tests -> SDK : span.set_attribute("exit_code", 0)

    Tests -> SDK : span.end()
    SDK -> Batch : buffer span

    alt Batch full or timeout
        Batch -> Exporter : export batch
        Exporter -> Weaver : OTLP protobuf (gRPC)

        note right of Weaver #WEAVER_COLOR
            Receives:
            ```protobuf
            ResourceSpans {
              resource: {
                attributes: [
                  {key:"service.name", value:"clnrm-test"}
                ]
              },
              scope_spans: [{
                spans: [{
                  name: "test_execution",
                  attributes: [
                    {key:"container.id", value:"abc123"},
                    {key:"test.isolated", value:true},
                    {key:"command", value:"echo hello"},
                    {key:"exit_code", value:0}
                  ]
                }]
              }]
            }
            ```
        end note

        Weaver -> Advisors : validate span against registry
        activate Advisors

        Advisors -> Advisors : check_required_attributes()
        note right
            From registry:
            ```yaml
            - id: container.id
              requirement_level: required
            - id: test.isolated
              requirement_level: required
            ```

            **Validation:**
            ✓ container.id present
            ✓ test.isolated present
            ✓ Both correct types
        end note

        alt All required attributes present
            Advisors --> Weaver : No violations #SUCCESS_COLOR
            Weaver -> Stats : record success
        else Required attribute missing
            Advisors --> Weaver : VIOLATION #FAIL_COLOR
            note right #FAIL_COLOR
                ```json
                {
                  "advice_level": "violation",
                  "advice_type": "required_attribute",
                  "message": "Required attribute 'container.id' missing",
                  "signal_name": "test_execution"
                }
                ```

                **This means container didn't run!**
                **Test result is FALSE POSITIVE!**
            end note
            Weaver -> Stats : record violation
        end

        deactivate Advisors

        Weaver --> Exporter : ACK
        Exporter --> Batch : export complete
    end

end

Tests -> SDK : shutdown()
SDK -> Batch : flush remaining
Batch -> Exporter : export final batch
Exporter -> Weaver : final spans

Tests --> Dev : Tests completed

deactivate Tests
deactivate Batch
deactivate SDK

== Validation Report Phase ==

Dev -> Weaver : kill -HUP (or wait timeout)
Weaver -> Stats : generate final statistics
activate Stats

Stats -> Stats : calculate_coverage()
note right
    ```rust
    registry_coverage =
        seen_registry_attrs /
        total_registry_attrs

    Example:
    15 attrs seen / 50 total = 0.30
    ```
end note

Stats -> Stats : count_violations()
Stats -> Stats : track_non_registry_attrs()

Stats --> Weaver : statistics report
deactivate Stats

Weaver -> Weaver : write live_check.json
note right #WEAVER_COLOR
    ```json
    {
      "samples": [ /* ... all spans ... */ ],
      "statistics": {
        "total_entities": 15,
        "total_advisories": 2,
        "advice_level_counts": {
          "violation": 0,
          "improvement": 2,
          "information": 0
        },
        "registry_coverage": 0.30,
        "seen_registry_attributes": {
          "container.id": 15,
          "test.isolated": 15,
          "command": 15,
          "exit_code": 15
        }
      }
    }
    ```
end note

alt Violations > 0
    Weaver -> Gate : exit_code = 1 #FAIL_COLOR
    Gate -> Gate : BLOCK MERGE ✋
    note right #FAIL_COLOR
        **CI/CD FAILS**

        Cannot merge PR.
        Cannot deploy to prod.
        MUST fix violations.

        **False positive detected!**
    end note
    Gate --> Dev : ❌ Validation FAILED
else No violations
    Weaver -> Gate : exit_code = 0 #SUCCESS_COLOR
    Gate -> Gate : ALLOW MERGE ✅
    note right #SUCCESS_COLOR
        **CI/CD PASSES**

        PR can be merged.
        Deploy to prod allowed.

        **Features proven to work!**
    end note
    Gate --> Dev : ✅ Validation PASSED
end

deactivate Weaver
deactivate Exporter

== The Critical Difference ==

note over Tests, Weaver #FFE5E5
    **WITHOUT Weaver Validation:**

    Test code:
    ```rust
    fn execute_in_container() -> Result<Output> {
        Ok(Output { stdout: "hello", exit_code: 0 })
        // FAKE! No container ran!
    }
    ```

    Test: assert_eq!(result.exit_code, 0)
    Result: ✅ PASS (FALSE POSITIVE)

    ❌ **Ships to production**
    ❌ **Breaks in prod**
    ❌ **No hermetic isolation**
end note

note over Tests, Weaver #E5FFE5
    **WITH Weaver Validation:**

    Same fake code above.
    Test still passes.

    **BUT:**
    Weaver checks telemetry:
    - Span: test_execution
    - Missing: container.id (REQUIRED)

    Advisor: VIOLATION
    Exit code: 1
    CI/CD: ❌ BLOCKED

    ✅ **Cannot ship without proof**
    ✅ **False positive detected**
    ✅ **Forces real implementation**
end note

@enduml
